{"id": "unknown-2026-11-05-012", "date": "2026-11-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "The Fraunhofer IPMS developed a compact 2K OLED microdisplay package with MIPI DSI-2", "content": "<p>Researchers at the <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/fraunhofer-institute-photonic-microsystems\">Fraunhofer IPMS</a> have developed a new compact package for the institute's 2K OLED microdisplay. The package integrates MIPI DSI-2 control and generates all the required display voltages.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sites/default/files/mcp-uploads/Fraunhofer-IPMS-2K-OLED-microdisplay-MIPI-DSI-2-package.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img class=\"align-center align-center\" src=\"https://www.oled-i", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/fraunhofer-ipms-developed-compact-2k-oled-microdisplay-package-mipi-dsi-2", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "canon-2026-11-05-013", "date": "2026-11-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": ["canon", "applied_materials"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.95, "reasons": ["多公司提及", "涉及財報"]}, "title": "Counterpoint: display equipment capex to fall 49% in 2027, Sunic System becomes the market's top supplier", "content": "<p>Counterpoint Research says that global display equipment capex will fall 49% in 2027, to $5.5 billion, after jumping 61% in 2026 to $10.8 billion. Korea's <a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sunic-system\">Sunic System</a> is expected to lead the market in 2027 with a 16% revenue share, ahead of Applied Materials (7%), Nikon (5%), Canon (3%) and Wonik IPS (3%). This would be the first time that a Korean equipment maker tops the display equipment market.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/sit", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/counterpoint-display-equipment-capex-fall-49-2027-sunic-system-becomes-markets", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "samsung_elec-2026-11-05-014", "date": "2026-11-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": ["samsung_elec"], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["oled_penetration"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Samsung Display targets gamers in China with QD-OLED certified internet cafes, plans 60 stores by the end of 2026", "content": "<p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-oled\">Samsung Display</a> announced that it is launching a promotion in China that designates internet cafes as \"QD-OLED certified stores\", in partnership with six monitor brands: AOC, ASUS, HKC, MSI, TitanArmy and ViewSonic. SDC completed its first 10 certified stores by the end of October, in major Chinese cities such as Beijing and Shanghai, and it plans to expand the program to 60 stores by the end of 2026.</p><a href=\"https://www.oled-info.com/s", "sources": [{"name": "oled_info", "url": "https://www.oled-info.com/samsung-display-targets-gamers-china-qd-oled-certified-internet-cafes-plans-60", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-05-015", "date": "2026-11-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Micron has paused a Taiwan cleanroom since October amid labor dispute, but keeps EUV plans", "content": "Micron has paused construction of a new cleanroom at its Fab 11E site in Taoyuan, Taiwan, since mid-October 2026, according to semiconductor supply chain sources. The company recently introduced a new quarterly bonus program tied to profits, but it still hasn't settled its dispute with the local union in Taoyuan, and no restart date has been set.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261105VL234/micron-taiwan-euv-cleanroom-labor.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-05-016", "date": "2026-11-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": -0.17, "keywords": ["increase", "[否定]expand", "slow"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Largan consolidates camera actuator unit as optical business expands into CPO", "content": "Largan Technology reported October revenue of NT$5.846 billion (US$178.1 million) on November 5, down 7.0% year-over-year, while moving to consolidate its camera actuator subsidiary and advance co-packaged optics (CPO) products. Revenue for the first 10 months of 2026 reached NT$50.705 billion, an increase of approximately 1% from the same period a year earlier, as the smartphone camera lens market entered its seasonal slowdown.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261105PD243/revenue-camera-cpo-subsidiary-2027.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-05-017", "date": "2026-11-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["[否定]growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Foxconn October revenue tops NT$1.3T on consumer and AI demand", "content": "Foxconn reported October 2026 revenue of NT$1.3053 trillion (US$39.8 billion), up 12.66% from September and 45.73% from a year earlier, as consumer smart products, computer terminals, components and other products posted strong growth. The result marked another month in which revenue exceeded NT$1 trillion. According to <em>DIGITIMES</em>, the performance was supported by stronger product pull-in activity and higher shipment prices.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261105PD242/foxconn-revenue-demand-2026-growth.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-05-018", "date": "2026-11-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.62, "keywords": ["record", "growth", "increase", "strong demand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Advantech sees high-double-digit growth through 2027, driven by AI and semiconductor equipment", "content": "Industrial PC leader Advantech reported record quarterly revenue and net profit for the third quarter of 2026, propelled by strong demand across semiconductor equipment, factory automation, and medical devices, alongside surging shipments of high-end edge AI systems. However, component price increases squeezed its gross margin down to 36.7%. Looking ahead, the company expects to maintain high-double-digit growth in both revenue and profit through 2027.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261105PD231/advantech-growth-equipment-pc-revenue.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-05-019", "date": "2026-11-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 1.0, "keywords": ["record"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "AI demand lifts Kyocera revenue as company raises forecast again", "content": "Japanese electronic components giant Kyocera reported record revenue of JPY1.08 trillion (approximately US$6.83 billion) for the first half of fiscal 2026 (April to September 2026), up 8.8% from the same period a year earlier. Operating profit and net income also grew by 32% to 56%. The results prompted Kyocera to raise its fiscal 2026 outlook for the second time, increasing its full-year revenue forecast to JPY2.12 trillion, 9% above its initial projection.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261105PD200/kyocera-revenue-demand-forecast-electronics.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-05-020", "date": "2026-11-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["slow"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "Beijing restricts equity listings amid market slump as YMTC pauses its stock market debut", "content": "Beijing has instructed top securities firms and investment banks to pause initial public offerings and restrict large-scale share sales by major shareholders. Reporting by <em>The Wall Street Journal</em> reveals that the China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) issued \"window guidance\" to slow equity supply and stem a prolonged market sell-off.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261105VL223/ymtc-beijing-stock-market-investment-2027.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-05-021", "date": "2026-11-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.75, "keywords": ["record", "growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.9, "reasons": ["涉及財報", "情緒極端"]}, "title": "Qisda revenue rises 13% in October as AI businesses accelerate", "content": "Qisda posted October consolidated revenue of NT$19.39 billion (US$590.8 million), up 13.47% year-over-year but down 1.85% from September, as its AI infrastructure, AI solutions, and smart manufacturing, and AI healthcare businesses all recorded double-digit growth from a year earlier.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261105PD225/revenue-qisda-healthcare-2026-infrastructure.html", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-11-05-022", "date": "2026-11-05", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 11, "week": 45, "weekday": "Thu"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "CHT ICT orders surge 84% as 3Q26 results beat guidance", "content": "Chunghwa Telecom (CHT) reported consolidated revenue of NT$675.9 billion (US$2.06 billion) for the third quarter of 2026, up 16.7% year over year, with revenue, operating profit, net income attributable to shareholders, and earnings per share all exceeding the high end of its financial forecast.", "sources": [{"name": "digitimes_display", "url": "https://www.digitimes.com/news/a20261105PD201/cht-revenue-profit-growth-operating-profit.html", "type": "rss"}]}
